  "decision_conditions": [
    "Under the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended), in the opinion of the Local Planning Authority, there is sufficient evidence to demonstrate that the ground floor premises, no. 8-10 Rowland Place, has been in continuous and uninterrupted Class A Use and, following the abolition of Class A on 01.09.2020, Class E use for a period of at least 10 years prior to the date of this application. In planning terms, the lawful use of the premises is therefore Class E, and as such any subsequent future conversion to another Class E Use would not require planning permission."
